For kernel recovery, the rule in recover_json_object says: 'The object scored is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one, else the last top-level object in the text', and later: 'A candidate that parses as strict JSON, or as JSON with repeated keys resolved last-wins, is scoreable; one that does not (a float, for instance) is passed over'. The original text is a fence containing A followed by S, so the only fenced candidate is A and the scored object is A. The rewritten text adds a later fence containing a float. The last fenced candidate is the float, but it is not scoreable and is passed over; the last scoreable fenced candidate is A, so the scored object remains A. Thus the check's answer is unchanged.